The magnitude of the $n$-th term is $|a_n| = \sqrt{(n - 2016)^2 + (n + 13)^2}$. To find the smallest magnitude, we need to find the value of $n$ that minimizes this expression.

The expression $(n - 2016)^2 + (n + 13)^2$ is minimized when the line through $(n - 2016, n + 13)$ and the origin is perpendicular to the line through $(n - 2016, n + 13)$ and $(n - 2016 + 1, n + 13 + 1) = (n - 2015, n + 14)$.

