9 km/hr * (1000 m/km) * (1/3600 h/min) * (1 min/60 min) = 9 * (1000/3600) m/s
9 km/hr = 9 * (1000/3600) m/s = 25 m/s

The train's speed is 45 km/hr. To convert this to m/s, we multiply by the conversion factor 1000 meters/km and 1/3600 hours/hour:
45 km/hr * (1000 m/km) * (1/3600 h/min) * (1 min/60 min) = 45 * (1000/3600) m/s
45 km/hr = 45 * (1000/3600) m/s = 12.5 m/s

The train is running in the same direction as the jogger, so the relative speed between the train and the jogger is the difference in their speeds:
Relative speed = Train's speed - Jogger's speed
