Distance = Relative speed * Time
Distance = 10 m/s * 25 s
Distance = 250 m

This distance is the sum of the length of the train and the initial distance between the train and the jogger, which is 150 m. Therefore, the length of the train is:
Length of train = Distance - Initial distance
