   \[
   G_m = \frac{G \cdot m}{r_m^2}
   \]
   where \(G\) is the gravitational constant (\(1.008 \times 10^8 \text{ m}^2/\text{s}^2\)), \(m\) is the Earth's mass (\(5.9761 \times 10^{24} \text{ kg}\)), and \(r_m\) is the mean radius.

