","(a) The force \( F \) exerted by the electric field on the proton is given by:  
\[
F = kF_e = (1.60 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{C}) \times (500 \, \text{N/C}) = 800 \times 10^{-19} \, \text{N} = 8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}
\]  
Using Newton's second law, \( F = mv \), we can find the acceleration \( a \):  
\[
a = \frac{F}{m} = \frac{8.00 \times 10^{-17} \, \text{N}}{1.67 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{kg}} \approx 4.81 \, \text{m/s}^2
\]  
Thus, the magnitude of the acceleration of the proton is \(\boxed{4.81 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).  

(b) Using the kinematic equation \( v = v_0 + at \), where \( v_0 = 0 \) (since the projectile starts at rest), we can solve for \( t \):  
\[
v = v_0 + at \implies t = \frac{v - v_0}{a} = \frac{35,000 \, \text{m/s} - 0 \, \text{m/s}}{4.81 \, \text{m/s}^2} \approx 7266.5 \, \text{s}
\]  
