- \( B \) is the magnetic force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force force field strength (in Newtons/second)
- \( I \) is the current applied to the loop (in Newtons)
- \( r \) is the radius of the circular loop (in meters)

Substituting the given values:
\[
B = \frac{1}{2} \pi \frac{1 \, \text{A}}{0.2 \, \text{m}}
\]

\[
B = \frac{\pi}{0.4} \, \text{N/m}
\]

\[
B \approx 7.85 \, \text{N/m}
\]

